.TH EMERGE 1 "2026" "aura-emerge 1.27.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emerge \- Portage-like command-line interface to Arch Linux, built on Aura
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emerge
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIaction\fR] [\fIpackage\fR | \fI@set\fR] [...]
.br
.B emerge
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIaction\fR] \fB@world\fR
.br
.B emerge
\fB\-\-sync\fR | \fB\-\-info\fR | \fB\-\-list\-sets\fR
.br
.B emerge \-\-resume
[\fB\-\-pretend\fR | \fB\-\-ask\fR | \fB\-\-skipfirst\fR]
.br
.B emerge \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aura-emerge
is a Gentoo\-style
.BR emerge (1)
wrapper for Arch Linux, built on top of
.BR aura (8).
It tracks every explicitly requested package in a single file,
.IR /etc/emerge/world.set ,
so the set of "things I actually asked for" survives independently of
whatever pacman's own dependency graph currently looks like.
.PP
Unlike a bare
.B pacman \-Syu
or
.BR "aura \-Syu \-Au" ,
.B emerge
distinguishes between three different operations that Gentoo users
expect to be different things:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
refreshing the package databases (\fB\-\-sync\fR),
.IP \(bu 2
upgrading everything already installed (\fB\-u\fR / \fB\-u @world\fR),
.IP \(bu 2
and making sure a machine actually \fIhas\fR everything it's supposed
to have (bare \fB@world\fR) \(em the operation this version introduces,
described in detail below.
.RE
.SH "PACKAGE ATOMS AND @world"
Every package
.B emerge
installs through the normal install path is recorded in
.I world.set
as
.IR repo/name ,
e.g.
.IR extra/firefox ", " aur/ayugram\-desktop\-bin ", or " abs/nano\-custom .
The prefix records where the package came from, so it can be
reinstalled from the same place later without guessing.
.SS "Bare @world (no \-u): declarative provisioning"
.B emerge @world
reads
.I world.set
and installs whatever it lists that isn't already on this system.
Packages already installed are left completely alone \(em nothing is
upgraded, nothing is reinstalled, nothing is removed. Each entry's
recorded prefix decides how it's installed:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
official-repo entries are installed via
.BR "aura \-S \-\-needed" ;
.IP \(bu 2
.I aur/
entries via
.BR "aura \-A \-\-needed" ,
after the usual PKGBUILD/.install scan;
.IP \(bu 2
.I abs/
entries (locally built from ABS) cannot be reproduced unattended and
are listed with a pointer to run
.B emerge <pkg> \-\-abs
yourself;
.IP \(bu 2
entries with no resolvable source
.RI ( Err/
or a bare name) are listed as needing manual attention.
.RE
.PP
This is the "move to a new machine and get everything back" operation:
copy (or symlink, or dotfiles-track)
.I /etc/emerge/world.set
onto a freshly installed system and run
.B emerge @world
to pull in the whole package set in one shot, official repos and AUR
alike \(em roughly what a NixOS user gets from applying their
configuration on a new host.
.PP
If named packages are given alongside
.BR @world ,
e.g.
.BR "emerge nano @world" ,
those packages are installed first (and added to
.IR world.set ,
as usual), and the remainder of
.I world.set
is then provisioned the same way as the bare form.
.SS "\-u @world / \-u: full system upgrade"
.B emerge \-u @world
(or plain
.BR "emerge \-u" )
is the Gentoo
.B emerge \-u @world
equivalent: it upgrades everything already installed \(em official
repos via
.BR "aura \-Syu" ,
then AUR packages via
.BR "aura \-Au" .
It does not consult
.I world.set
at all; this is a pure "bring the currently installed set up to date"
operation, independent of what's tracked as explicitly wanted.
.SS "\-\-sync: database refresh"
.B emerge \-\-sync
runs
.B aura \-Sy
(or
.B \-Syy
with
.BR \-\-refresh ),
refreshing the package databases without installing or upgrading
anything, unless packages or
.B @world
are also given, in which case it falls through to the matching
install/upgrade/provision step afterward.
.SH "CUSTOM SETS"
Beyond
.B @world
and
.BR @preserved\-rebuild ,
.B emerge
supports arbitrary named sets: a file
.IB /etc/emerge/sets.d/ name .set
is invoked on the command line as
.BI @ name
(e.g.
.I /etc/emerge/sets.d/game\-kit.set
as
.BR @game\-kit ).
.PP
A set file holds one package atom per line; blank lines and lines
starting with
.B #
are ignored. A set can be combined with other sets and with plain
package names in the same invocation, e.g.:
.PP
.RS
.nf
emerge @game\-kit @dev\-tools neovim
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B \-\-list\-sets
prints every set currently available (\fB@world\fR,
\fB@preserved\-rebuild\fR, and one line per
.I sets.d/*.set
file) \(em this is also what shell completion calls behind the scenes
so that
.B "emerge @<TAB>"
offers real set names instead of just the two built-in ones.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Actions
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-search
Search for packages (official repos + AUR).
.TP
.B \-\-searchdesc
Search package descriptions.
.TP
.B \-sv
Detailed package info (\fBaura \-Si\fR / \fB\-Ai\fR).
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-update
Full system upgrade; see "\-u @world / \-u" above.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-unmerge
Remove specific packages and drop them from world.set.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-depclean
Remove orphaned packages (skips anything tracked in world.set).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretend
Dry run \(em show what would happen without doing it.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ask
Ask for confirmation before applying changes.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-oneshot
Install as a dependency; does not touch world.set.
.TP
.B \-\-sync
Sync package databases; see "\-\-sync" above.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Force\-refresh databases even if already current (\fBpacman \-Syy\fR);
used with \fB\-\-sync\fR or \fB\-u\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-info
Show system info, mirroring Gentoo's \fBemerge \-\-info\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-select
Add packages to world.set without installing them.
.TP
.B \-\-deselect
Remove packages from world.set without unmerging them.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
Remove installed packages that are not tracked in world.set.
.TP
.B \-\-regen
Regenerate pacman's file-list metadata cache (\fBpacman \-Fy\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-regen\-world
Re\-resolve repository prefixes for every entry in world.set.
.TP
.B \-\-regen\-world\-from\-explicit
One\-time migration: seed world.set from every currently
explicitly\-installed package (\fBpacman \-Qeq\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Resume the last interrupted install/\fB@world\fR operation.
.TP
.B \-\-skipfirst
Used with \fB\-\-resume\fR: skip the first package in the resumed list.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-sets
List available \fB@\fR sets; see "CUSTOM SETS" above.
.SS "Install source selection"
.TP
.B \-\-aur
Force installation from the AUR only.
.TP
.B \-\-only\-repos
Only use official repos; never search or install from the AUR.
.TP
.B \-\-abs
Build from ABS (Arch Build System) source via
.BR asp (1).
.TP
.B \-\-skippgp
Skip PGP signature checks when building from ABS.
.TP
.B \-\-autopgp
Automatically import missing PGP keys (from \fBvalidpgpkeys\fR) from a
trusted keyserver when building with \fB\-\-abs\fR, without prompting.
.TP
.B \-\-edit
Edit the PKGBUILD before building \(em opens \fB$EDITOR\fR for
\fB\-\-abs\fR, or passes \fBaura\fR's own \fB\-\-hotedit\fR for AUR builds.
.SS "Other"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output / detailed info in search mode.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-noreplace
Do not reinstall if already installed (\fBpacman \-\-needed\fR).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a brief usage summary.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.PP
A number of Gentoo/Portage-compatibility flags
.RI ( "\-\-deep, \-\-newuse, \-\-emptytree, \-\-with\-bdeps, \-\-verbose\-conflicts" ,
etc.) are accepted for muscle-memory compatibility and are otherwise
no-ops.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/emerge/world.set
Every explicitly\-installed package, one
.I repo/name
atom per line. Edit it by hand if you like \(em it's just a text file.
.TP
.I /etc/emerge/sets.d/*.set
Custom package sets; see "CUSTOM SETS" above.
.TP
.I /etc/emerge/resume.state
Saved argv\-equivalent of the last interrupted install/\fB@world\fR
operation, consumed by \fB\-\-resume\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B emerge neovim
Install neovim (official repos, falls back to AUR).
.TP
.B emerge neovim\-git \-\-aur
Install explicitly from the AUR.
.TP
.B emerge @world
On a freshly installed machine with a populated
.IR world.set ,
install everything it lists that's still missing.
.TP
.B emerge \-u @world
Upgrade the whole system, official repos and AUR alike.
.TP
.B emerge @game\-kit
Install every package listed in
.IR /etc/emerge/sets.d/game\-kit.set .
.TP
.B emerge \-\-prune
Remove anything installed that isn't tracked in
.IR world.set .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR aura (8),
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makepkg (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Undercat037 \(em
